.TH "PB-SESSION-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-session-list - List durable terminal sessions


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb session list [environment] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List durable terminal sessions

.PP
List durable sessions with automatic application title or foreground process and current directory where observed. “Started in” labels the launch directory when current metadata is unavailable. --wide adds the session ID; choose an exact session ID for attach, rename, close, or sharing.

.PP
Terminal sessions persist independently of a single connection and can be reattached after a disconnect. Sharing grants explicit access to a named session. Closing, deleting, and removing a participant have different effects; inspect the selected session before acting.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--closed\fP[=false]
	filter explicitly by closed state

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--owner\fP=""
	filter owner: mine, shared, or an authorized account ID

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by resource name or ID

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by resource state

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	include immutable IDs


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-session(1)\fP
